{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793478767,"nonce":"DAXQRCzsQHmG5bBsSDQZN1vGK20=","title":"Source Control offers to initialize a repository instead of raising an error","message":"A folder that is not a Git repository made the Source Control view raise an error toast ('open repository: could not find repository at ...'). The view now says there is no repository and offers Initialize Repository, as the person's own act. The Git extension binds git_repository_init, reports a missing repository as a plain state, and the sidebar shows the option. Covered by the native Git checks and the Git sidebar checks. The Cloud Sync sidebar's Initialize Git button runs git init the same way.","files":null}]}